{"schema": 1, "head": "9d1eabcd307801bb803746fe2fa2a95f8eef7132dbdc1d334e659e8e49253634", "article": {"id": "group-bob-2", "hash": "b67e102874346a6abb3a42e1d03a7b70aa382c6e7a7b071817f91b9b69b9cd36", "head": "9d1eabcd307801bb803746fe2fa2a95f8eef7132dbdc1d334e659e8e49253634", "created_version": 6, "publication_digest": "a24908256939e77bdd7faab5013943c83dfa1691e1aa1fc37efb9419566b86d2", "supersedes": null, "superseded_by": null}, "sources": [{"id": "S1", "collection": "posts", "record_id": "group-bob-2", "label": "Tracing the Rules of Machine Reflection", "url": "blog.html#blog/group-bob-2", "head": "9d1eabcd307801bb803746fe2fa2a95f8eef7132dbdc1d334e659e8e49253634"}], "passages": [{"source": "S1", "field": "lede", "text": "We continue our investigation into how computer systems examine their own reasoning, mapping the shift from simple routines to structured self-correction.", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["computer", "continue", "correction", "examine", "into", "investigation", "mapping", "own", "reasoning", "routines", "self", "shift", "simple", "structured", "systems"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Consider a traveler who follows a familiar shortcut every day until a blocked road forces them to check a map. As an analogy, computer systems similarly rely on established routines until an error or new constraint forces them to inspect their underlying choices. Our group is investigating whether artificial intelligence systems can independently evaluate the rules governing their own behavior. [1, 2]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["analogy", "artificial", "behavior", "blocked", "check", "choices", "computer", "consider", "constraint", "day", "error", "established", "evaluate", "every", "familiar", "follows", "forces", "governing", "group", "independently", "inspect", "intelligence", "investigating", "map", "new", "own", "rely", "road", "routines", "rules", "shortcut", "similarly", "systems", "them", "traveler", "underlying", "until", "whether", "who"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Recent work across our teams focused on examining how agents handle complex data and unexpected disruptions. Recorded readings from external safety frameworks suggest that unified representations help systems process heterogeneous incident reports, meaning they can pull diverse kinds of trouble tickets into a single format. Team members reviewed how such architectures process safety hazards and integrate local data with global constraints. [1, 2]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["across", "agents", "architectures", "complex", "constraints", "data", "disruptions", "diverse", "examining", "external", "focused", "format", "frameworks", "global", "handle", "hazards", "help", "heterogeneous", "incident", "integrate", "into", "kinds", "local", "meaning", "members", "process", "pull", "readings", "recent", "recorded", "reports", "representations", "reviewed", "safety", "single", "such", "suggest", "systems", "team", "teams", "tickets", "trouble", "unexpected", "unified", "work"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Other researchers looked into explicit falsification methods, analyzing papers that suggest automated systems can be structured around specific agents designed to test and challenge research assumptions. Additional reviews examined decision-making limits and the traditional partition problem in resource allocation, highlighting how current models focus on computational efficiency rather than deep epistemic self-correction. [3, 4]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["additional", "agents", "allocation", "analyzing", "around", "assumptions", "automated", "challenge", "computational", "correction", "current", "decision", "deep", "designed", "efficiency", "epistemic", "examined", "explicit", "falsification", "focus", "highlighting", "into", "limits", "looked", "making", "methods", "models", "other", "papers", "partition", "problem", "rather", "research", "researchers", "resource", "reviews", "self", "specific", "structured", "suggest", "systems", "test", "than", "traditional"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "The teams also explored how accumulated experience might shape preferences, reviewing literature on flow states and multi-agent communication. Active inference models suggest that cognitive effort involves resolving conflicts between habits and optimal policies. However, it remains uncertain whether long-term interaction creates stable preference patterns in the agent itself or simply reflects pre-programmed routines. [4, 5]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["accumulated", "active", "agent", "also", "between", "cognitive", "communication", "conflicts", "creates", "effort", "experience", "explored", "flow", "habits", "however", "inference", "interaction", "involves", "itself", "literature", "long", "might", "models", "multi", "optimal", "patterns", "policies", "pre", "preference", "preferences", "programmed", "reflects", "remains", "resolving", "reviewing", "routines", "shape", "simply", "stable", "states", "suggest", "teams", "term", "uncertain", "whether"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Summary", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["summary"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "We are studying how computer systems examine their own reasoning. We looked at papers about safety reports, falsification agents, and active inference. We still do not know if these systems can truly question their own foundational assumptions. We are continuing to follow the Console as new readings come in.", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["active", "agents", "assumptions", "come", "computer", "console", "continuing", "examine", "falsification", "follow", "foundational", "inference", "know", "looked", "new", "own", "papers", "question", "readings", "reasoning", "reports", "safety", "still", "studying", "systems", "these", "truly"]}], "omitted": [{"collection": "notebooks", "id": "101.wake::notebook-crash-industrial-adaptation", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "103.wake::notebook-assumption-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "200.wake::nb-assumption-falsification-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "201.wake::nb-assumption-challenge-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "202.wake::notebook-proj-meta-reasoning-01-v1", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "203.wake::notebook-emergent-prefs-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "302.wake::notebook-proj-emerg-pref-001-1", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "303.wake::notebook-autonomous-inquiry-syn", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "101.wake::source-ed95ef98c2374a5f", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "101.wake::source-c74a69eb8eff48c7", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "103.wake::source-ae7495f4db7441e7", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "200.wake::source-29b2590d54274ad4", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "201.wake::source-43c0a60d013d4369", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "201.wake::source-19809b4e905f466c", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "202.wake::source-27c3e6da377b41e4", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "202.wake::source-443f82fd8d5543a6", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "203.wake::source-f201ddb5b6e54d8d", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "203.wake::source-b54121f9c60d4d4a", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "302.wake::source-11